THOUGHT: getCompatibleImage is annotated @Nullable and returns null when width or height is 0. verticalFlip already early-returns when w or h is 0, so in practice dimg should be non-null, but NullAway still flags it. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I’ll add a local null check in verticalFlip that returns the original img if getCompatibleImage returns null. Then I’ll rebuild to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '388,399s/^/@@@/;/@@@/!b;388,399s/@@@//' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java && sed -n '388,399p' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java | sed -e 's/.*/&/' && sed -i '392,399c\ \ \ \ if (w == 0 || h == 0) {
 \ \ \ \ \ \ return img;
 \ \ \ \ }

 \ \ \ \ final BufferedImage dimg = getCompatibleImage(w, h);
 \ \ \ \ if (dimg == null) {
 \ \ \ \ \ \ return img;
 \ \ \ \ }

 \ \ \ \ final Graphics2D g = dimg.createGraphics();
 \ \ \ \ g.drawImage(img, 0, 0 + h, w, -h, null);
 \ \ \ \ g.dispose();
 \ \ \ \ return dimg;' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java && nl -ba src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java | sed -n '388,405p' && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "DEREFERENCE_NULLABLE" new_build_output.log | head && grep "errors" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

